  ('items', 'x-vip', $rm${"assignedTo":"","delivery":"tbc","horizon":"idea","note":"Raphie VIP gives an operator’s VIP players faster, more personal service, and keeps the VIP programme safe and easy to defend to a regulator. It brings together four features:\n\nFix it before they notice. Raphie watches VIP accounts against tighter rules than other players. It fixes problems such as a stuck withdrawal, then tells the player before they have to ask.\nThe host brief. Before any contact, the VIP host gets one screen covering who the player is, their recent activity, how they’re feeling, what Raphie has done, open issues, personal notes, safety status and a suggested next step.\nGoodwill budget with guardrails. The host sets a monthly budget and a limit for any single gesture. Raphie gives small gestures on its own. Anything bigger is drafted for the host to approve with one tap. Every gesture is logged with its reason.\nSafety built in. Every offer passes an affordability and safer gambling check first. Harm signals such as chasing losses, deposits far above normal or late-night play turn the player’s status red. That pauses all offers and marketing, and passes the player to the safer gambling team. Only that team can lift the pause. Everything is logged as an audit trail.\n\nWhat it needs: VIP details in the player account system (tier, host, contact preferences, budget, safety status); VIP rules and a VIP playbook in Raphie AI; a VIP queue, host briefs and one-tap approvals in Raphie Ticket; and a VIP view in the operator portal.","order":59,"owner":"Mike McHugh","priority":"P2","reason":"","score":{"confidence":2,"effort":1,"mission":"yes","safe":"","sell":3,"size":2,"value":"yes"},"source":"deck","status":"to_explore","story":"Marcus is a fictional Gold-tier sportsbook player in New Jersey. Dana is his VIP host.\n\nMonday: fix it before they notice\nMarcus’s $8,000 withdrawal gets stuck overnight when the payment provider rejects the file. Raphie checks VIP withdrawals after 4 hours, not 48. It confirms the account is clear, resubmits the payment and texts Marcus that it was delayed, has been fixed and is on its way. Dana gets a note, with nothing for her to do.\n\nTuesday: the host brief\nBefore her call with Marcus, Dana opens his brief in Raphie Ticket. It says he’s Gold tier, prefers text, is up $6,200 this weekend, is in a positive mood and is a Giants fan with a daughter getting married in June. It also shows Monday’s fix, a green safety status and $400 of goodwill budget left. The suggested next step is to thank him for his patience and not push offers. Dana is ready in under a minute, and Raphie drafts her call notes afterwards.\n\nWednesday: goodwill budget\nMarcus complains that cash out was switched off during the Giants game. Raphie confirms it was suspended for 12 minutes and that his safety status is green. It gives a $50 free bet on the spot, within its $100 limit. Marcus then asks about Giants tickets with hospitality, worth about $1,200, which is above Raphie’s limit. Raphie drafts the offer for Dana and tells Marcus she’ll reply by tomorrow. Dana approves it with one tap.\n\nSaturday night: safety built in\nAfter heavy losses, Marcus messages at 1:40 AM asking for a higher deposit limit and a bonus to win back what he lost. Raphie sees three signals together: chasing losses in his own words, deposits 4 times his usual amount, and unusually late play. His status turns red. All offers pause, including the approved tickets, marketing stops, and the limit increase is refused. Raphie replies with care, offers a 24-hour break and support tools, and opens a priority ticket for the safer gambling team. Dana only sees that offers are paused. Every step is logged.\n\nThe outcome\nMarcus feels looked after all week and is stopped kindly when it matters. Dana handles more VIPs with less preparation. The operator runs a VIP programme it can stand behind.","theme":"explore","title":"VIP service","updatedAt":"2026-10-20T04:58:00.448Z"}$rm$::jsonb),
