  ('items', 'token-billing', $rm${"assignedTo":"","delivery":"internal","docUrl":"https://claude.ai/artifact/RTpZLWwXPA1QD4raDv4Z7b","horizon":"idea","note":"To be reviewed. Two parts: (1) every model call goes through one gateway that records tokens and cost per customer, conversation and step (counts and IDs only, never message text); (2) a clear billable-resolution definition, exclusions and agreed escalations written into the MSA. Phases: define, track tokens, resolution ledger and billing export, run side by side for one customer for a month, MSA template, show in Raphie Hub. Edge cases still to decide are listed in the doc.","order":950,"owner":"Mike McHugh","priority":"","reason":"","review":true,"source":"meeting","story":"An operator's finance team gets a monthly statement of billable resolutions by ticket ID, defined in the MSA: tickets Raphie handled end to end, closed and not reopened within 7 days, plus any agreed escalations at 99 cents each. Disputes are credited automatically. Raphie's own team sees token cost and margin per resolution for every customer.","theme":"hub","title":"Token tracking and billable resolutions","updatedAt":"2026-10-26T06:10:00Z"}$rm$::jsonb),
